<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/039U">Remark <span data-tag="039U">7.3.5.4</span>.</a> In the situation of Corollary <a data-tag="039T" href="/tag/039T">7.3.5.3</a>, suppose we are given a functor $F: \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ and a natural transformation $\beta : F_0 \rightarrow F \circ U$. Then $\beta $ exhibits $F$ as a left Kan extension of $F$ along $U$ if and only if, for every object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the induced natural transformation $\beta _{C}: F_0 |_{ \mathscr {G}(C) } \rightarrow \underline{ F(C) }$ exhibits $F(C)$ as a colimit of the diagram $F_0 |_{ \mathscr {G}(C)}$ </p>
